# Security Standards

See `docs/13-security-and-threat-model.md`. Security is layered mitigations — never claim 100% security.

## Auth

- Hash passwords with Argon2id.
- Short-lived access JWTs; rotating refresh tokens; store refresh token hashes server-side; revoke on logout/password change.
- Web auth: HTTP-only access/refresh cookies + CSRF (`X-CSRF-Token` double-submit); never `localStorage` for tokens (DEC-012).
- Rate-limit login, registration, and password-reset endpoints.
- Unique WhatsApp number; document (do not silently skip) trial-abuse limits.

## Authorization

- RBAC on every protected endpoint.
- Prevent IDOR: authorize by ownership or admin role.
- Answer privacy is a **backend** requirement: omit `correctOptionId` / `isCorrect` / `explanation` when the caller lacks premium entitlement.

## Input & output

- Validate and sanitize all inputs.
- Parameterized queries via Prisma only.
- Escape/encode output; CSP-friendly frontend practices.
- CSRF protection where cookie-based auth applies.

## Files

- Server-side or signed Cloudinary uploads only.
- MIME + size validation; ownership checks; secure delete.
- Private/authenticated delivery or short-lived signed URLs for restricted assets.

## Ops

- Secrets only in env / secret store; never commit.
- Do not expose Postgres or Redis publicly.
- Audit sensitive admin actions.
- Keep dependencies patched; review advisories in CI when available.
